  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "The mean of three numbers is \\(10\\) more than the least of the numbers and \\(15\\) less than the greatest. The median of the three numbers is \\(5.\\) What is their sum?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "For three numbers in increasing order, the median is the middle number. Let their mean be \\(m\\). The least number is therefore \\(m-10\\), the middle number is \\(5\\), and the greatest number is \\(m+15\\).\n\nTheir sum must be three times their mean, so\n\\[\n(m-10)+5+(m+15)=3m.\n\\]\nCombining terms gives \\(2m+10=3m\\), hence \\(m=10\\). The numbers are \\(0,5,25\\), which have the required order and mean. Their sum is \\(3\\cdot10=\\boxed{30}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
